WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.560
Today, we are talking about the Valentine's Day episode.
今天，我们要聊的是情人节那一集。

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.620
I am so excited for this one.
我太期待这一集了。

10
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.220
Me too.
我也是。

11
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.700
I liked this one so much, I watched it an extra time in my prep.
我太喜欢这一集了，备课时我又多看了一遍。

12
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:34.760
I did too.
我也是。

13
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.720
Just for pleasure.
纯粹是为了享受。

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.340
I did too.
我也是。

15
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.680
My husband Josh was like, babe, how many times are you going to watch that episode?
我丈夫乔什问我：宝贝，你到底要看多少遍那一集？

16
00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.000
I was like, I am really enjoying it.
我说：我真的很享受看它。

17
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.500
I think this one sneaked up on me because there are certain episodes that I remember as being favorites.
我觉得这一集让我感到意外，因为有些集数我一直记得是我的最爱。

18
00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:47.900
Yeah.
是啊。

19
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.560
And this one was not on my radar.
而这一集之前并不在我的关注名单里。

20
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.600
And then I watched it and so many memories came back too.
但看完之后，好多回忆都涌上心头。

21
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:53.840
So many.
太多了。

22
00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.460
Okay, this is a goodie.
好吧，这集真的很棒。

23
00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.400
This is Season 2, Episode 16, written by Mike Schur and directed by Greg Daniels.
这是第二季第16集，由迈克·舒尔编剧，格雷格·丹尼尔斯执导。

24
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.360
I mean, honestly, that's all you need to know right there.
说实话，光看这些信息就足够了。

25
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.280
That's like the super team.
这简直是梦之队。

26
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.940
Yeah, of course this is a great one.
没错，这集当然会很精彩。

27
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.620
All right, I'll give a summary.
好了，我来做个总结。

28
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.620
It's Valentine's Day at Dunder Mifflin.
邓德·米夫林公司迎来了情人节。

29
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.240
Michael has to go to the corporate offices in New York.
迈克尔必须去纽约的公司总部。

30
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.400
He has to meet and do a presentation for the new CFO, Chief Financial Officer.
他要与新任首席财务官（CFO）会面并进行演示。

31
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.340
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

32
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:22.980
It is.
确实。

33
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.700
And he's going to be there with Jan on Valentine's Day.
而且他要在情人节那天和简待在一起。

34
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.400
Oh, no.
噢，不。

35
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:35.180
Back at the office, Phyllis is overwhelmed by gifts from her boyfriend, Bob Vance, at Vance Refrigeration.
在办公室这边，菲利斯被她男友——万斯制冷公司的鲍勃·万斯送的礼物淹没了。

36
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.940
They just come all day, these gifts.
这些礼物一整天都在送来。

37
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:37.440
All day.
一整天。

38
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.980
Pam patiently waits for a gift from Roy that never comes.
帕姆耐心地等待着罗伊送来的礼物，但礼物始终没出现。

39
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.140
No, no.
没有，根本没有。

40
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.640
And she really dolled herself up.
而且她还特意精心打扮了一番。

41
00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:46.400
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

42
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.500
That's my fast fact number one, Angela.
安吉拉，这是我的第一个速览小知识。

43
00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:48.880
Do it.
快说。

44
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:49.340
Do it.
快说。

45
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.080
Fan question from Baltimore Ashley.
来自巴尔的摩的阿什莉的粉丝提问。

46
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.940
What was the thought process behind Pam's hair for this episode?
这一集中帕姆的发型设计思路是什么？

47
00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.220
Was there another special meeting?
还有别的特别会议吗？

48
00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.380
I bet there was.
我敢说肯定有。

49
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

50
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:00.920
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

51
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:07.080
I also got similar questions from Casey McMillan and many other people asking if there was a special
凯西·麦克米伦和许多其他人也问过我类似的问题，问是不是专门为帕姆的发型开过一个

52
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.240
meeting for Pam's hair.
特别会议。

53
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.380
There was more than a meeting.
那可不止是一个会议。

54
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.060
It was like the Joint Chiefs of Staff came together for your hair.
简直就像参谋长联席会议为了你的发型聚在了一起。

55
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:21.800
So the thought process here was that Pam and Jim in this episode, they're going to be a bit estranged.
所以当时的构思是，帕姆和吉姆在这一集中会有些疏远。

56
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:29.760
So wouldn't it be an extra nail in the coffin for Jim if Pam just looked super duper cute?
那么如果帕姆看起来超级可爱，对吉姆来说岂不是雪上加霜？

57
00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.360
Right.
没错。

58
00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.680
So we thought, can we please do something different with her hair?
所以我们想，能不能在她的发型上做点不一样的尝试？

59
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:47.840
I had a MySpace blog at the time and I wrote about my hair and I said that Kim Ferry and I worked for weeks on different versions of this look.
我当时有个MySpace博客，我在上面写到了我的发型，我说金·费里和我为了这个造型的不同版本研究了好几周。

60
00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:56.560
Well, knowing Kim Ferry like I do, like you do, she must have been so excited because she was so good at hair, but she never got to do much with our hair.
嗯，像我一样了解金·费里的人都知道，她当时一定很兴奋，因为她非常擅长做发型，但平时却没机会在我们的头发上大展身手。

61
00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:56.940
No.
没错。

62
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:57.560
Okay.
好吧。

63
00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.560
So here's what we tried.
所以我们尝试了这些方案。

64
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.260
We tried a ponytail, a barrette, and headbands.
我们试了马尾辫、发夹和发带。

65
00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:13.960
We took a picture of each choice and we presented them to Greg Daniels and he went through the photos and had to pick hairstyle and he picked the headband and there were various headbands.
我们给每个造型都拍了照，然后拿给格雷格·丹尼尔斯看，他翻看照片并从中挑选，最后选定了发带，而且当时有很多种发带。

66
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.040
I was going to say, were there 12 different headbands?
我正想问，是不是有12种不同的发带？

67
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:18.480
Yes.
是的。

68
00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.120
Yes.
没错。

69
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.160
So it was, and also ponytails, high pony, low pony, side pony.
确实是，还有马尾辫，高马尾、低马尾、侧马尾。

70
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.500
No side pony.
没有侧马尾。

71
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.140
Well, side pony shows up later at the art fair.
好吧，侧马尾后来在艺术展上出现了。

72
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.980
Um, I wore a side ponytail to my prom.
嗯，我参加毕业舞会时扎的就是侧马尾。

73
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.960
My, I think it was my, my senior year I did a side pony.
我记得是在我高三那年扎的侧马尾。

74
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.340
I was not cool, guys.
伙计们，我当时一点也不酷。

75
00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.000
You did a side pony to prom?
你扎着侧马尾去参加毕业舞会？

76
00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:39.520
Yeah.
对。

77
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:40.740
I did a side.
我扎了侧马尾。

78
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.360
Did you get that done at a salon or did you do that at home?
那是去沙龙做的，还是你自己在家弄的？

79
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.880
No, my mom did it.
不，是我妈帮我弄的。

80
00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:51.020
My mom did it and that was the year, the year before we had all had dates and none of us had a good time.
是我妈弄的，那年之前我们都有舞伴，但大家玩得都不开心。

81
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.140
My group of like really close girlfriends.
就是我那群非常要好的闺蜜。

82
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:53.420
Yeah.
是啊。

83
00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:58.420
So that was the year, the guys thought they were being really cool and they were like, we're not going to take dates this year.
所以那一年，男生们觉得自己很酷，他们说，我们今年不带舞伴去了。

84
00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.600
I went to a small school.
我读的是一所小学校。

85
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.600
And so the girls were like, fine.
所以女生们就说，行啊。

86
00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.660
And we had the best time.
结果我们玩得最开心。

87
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.860
Was that your senior prom?
那是你的毕业舞会吗？

88
00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.860
Our senior prom, I danced in a circle with all my girlfriends with a side ponytail.
我们的毕业舞会，我扎着侧马尾，和所有的闺蜜围成一圈跳舞。

89
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:13.460
Lady, I did an all girls prom for my senior prom too.
天哪，我的毕业舞会也是全女生参加的。

90
00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:13.980
You did.
真的吗？

91
00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.100
We would have been in the same dance circle.
那我们肯定会在同一个跳舞圈子里。

92
00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:16.820
We would have.
肯定会的。

93
00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.260
You would have loved my side pony.
你一定会喜欢我的侧马尾的。

94
00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.000
I have a card about that fast fact.
我有一张关于那个冷知识的卡片。

95
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:22.800
Tell it.
说来听听。

96
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.340
I mean, not only is it Pam's hair, Pam is wearing a pink sweater.
我是说，不仅是帕姆的发型，帕姆还穿着一件粉色毛衣。

97
00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.760
Her headband's pink.
她的发带是粉色的。

98
00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.420
She has a heart necklace on.
她戴着心形项链。

99
00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.260
She has pink earrings on.
她戴着粉色耳环。

100
00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.160
I mean.
我是说。

101
00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.480
Little pink dangle earrings.
粉色的小吊坠耳环。

102
00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:34.720
I know.
我知道。

103
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.000
The lady came, like she came to be noticed.
那位女士来了，感觉她是特意来引人注目的。

104
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:38.680
She did.
确实。

105
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.440
She's, I think a little lip gloss.
我觉得她还涂了点唇彩。

106
00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.060
Yes.
没错。

107
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.080
It was a whole look.
整体造型很完整。

108
00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:47.540
I have to say when I first saw myself on screen, I was a little bit like, oh.
我得说，当我第一次在屏幕上看到自己时，我有点……噢。

109
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.840
Oh, Pam went for it.
噢，帕姆豁出去了。

110
00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.660
Pam showed up today.
帕姆今天盛装出席了。

111
00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:56.460
And I mean, I mean, it's going to play out later in the episode, but like, Roy, come on.
我是说，我是说，这在剧集后面会体现出来，但是罗伊，拜托。

112
00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.100
This is someone who clearly wants a valentine.
这明显是一个想要情人节礼物的人。

113
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.100
So clearly.
太明显了。

114
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:00.920
No matter what she says.
不管她怎么说。

115
00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:01.240
Okay.
好的。

116
00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:01.560
Sorry.
抱歉。

117
00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.560
Fast fact number two.
快速事实之二。

118
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.660
Fast fact number two.
快速事实之二。

119
00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.200
A portion of this episode was shot in New York City.
这一集的部分内容是在纽约市拍摄的。

120
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.440
We got a lot of fan questions about this.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于此事的提问。

121
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.720
People wanted to know if we, did Steve stand in front of a green screen?
人们想知道我们……史蒂夫是站在绿幕前吗？

122
00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.220
Did we shoot on the streets of Los Angeles?
我们是在洛杉矶街头拍摄的吗？

123
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.100
No.
不是。

124
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.200
But there's more questions, Angela.
但还有更多问题，安吉拉。

125
00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:19.480
Okay.
好的。

126
00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.760
Fan question from Cora Louise.
来自科拉·路易斯的粉丝提问。

127
00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.200
How many crew members came to New York City?
有多少剧组成员去了纽约市？

128
00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:29.860
And Guava Aura asked, how long did it take to shoot this episode in New York?
还有瓜娃·奥拉问，在纽约拍摄这一集花了多长时间？

129
00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.360
And was the rest of the cast in California?
其他演员当时都在加州吗？

130
00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:33.640
Yes.
是的。

131
00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.260
We did not get to go.
我们没能去成。

132
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:35.940
We did not.
我们确实没去。

133
00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.120
We were all pretty bummed because it sounded like so much fun.
我们都很沮丧，因为听起来太好玩了。

134
00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.980
So I reached out to Randall Einhorn, our director of photography.
所以我联系了我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

135
00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:43.580
Jenna, you know I did this.
珍娜，你知道我这么做了。

136
00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.120
I know.
我知道。

137
00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.040
And you guys, she wouldn't tell me what he said.
你们知道吗，她不肯告诉我他说了什么。

138
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.840
She's got all this good information about the New York shoot and she made me wait.
她掌握了所有关于纽约拍摄的内幕消息，却让我等着。

139
00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.500
Well, this is something we do.
嗯，这是我们常做的事。

140
00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.320
We both love to like dig up nuggets of info and then we don't tell each other because
我们都喜欢挖掘信息碎片，然后不告诉对方，因为

141
00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.400
we want the surprise.
我们想要惊喜感。

142
00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.040
I know.
我知道。

143
00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.880
So I've been waiting like five days for this.
所以我为了这个已经等了五天了。

144
00:05:58.880 --> 00:05:59.160
Okay.
好的。

145
00:05:59.160 --> 00:05:59.740
Here we go.
开始了。

146
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:03.860
So I reached out to Randall and he said the crew in New York was just him and Greg and
所以我联系了兰德尔，他说在纽约的剧组只有他和格雷格，还有

147
00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.660
Steve that would go out on the street when they would film.
史蒂夫，他们拍摄时会走到街上。

148
00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:06.940
Yeah.
是的。

149
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:11.580
And in the van they had like I think two crew members that were New York based like because
而且在面包车里，我想他们有两名纽约当地的剧组成员，因为

150
00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.320
they had to do things by the rules, you know.
他们必须按规矩办事，你懂的。

151
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:18.480
And our line producer Kent Zabornak, but whenever the van doors would open, it would just be
还有我们的制片主任肯特·扎博纳克，但每当面包车门打开时，出来的就只有

152
00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.200
Greg, Steve, and Randall.
格雷格、史蒂夫和兰德尔。

153
00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:24.660
He said that this was right at the height of 40-year-old Virgin.
他说那正好是《四十岁的老处男》最火的时候。

154
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.580
It was the biggest movie in America.
那是全美最热门的电影。

155
00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.580
He said there was a billboard in Times Square where they were filming.
他说在他们拍摄的地方，时代广场上挂着一块广告牌。

156
00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.260
So he said the minute Steve would get out of the van, a crowd would form.
所以他说史蒂夫一从车里出来，人群就会围上来。

157
