But I thought it was interesting because the joke of our episode is kind of that Michael doesn't get what a local pizza joint is, but it did actually start as a local pizza joint.
但我认为这很有趣，因为我们这一集的笑点在于迈克尔不懂什么是本地披萨店，但它实际上确实是从一家本地披萨店起家的。

801
00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:15.100
It did start local.
它确实是从本地起家的。

802
00:31:15.520 --> 00:31:16.040
It did start local.
它确实是从本地开始的。

803
00:31:16.220 --> 00:31:17.420
Just not in Times Square.
只是不在时代广场。

804
00:31:17.600 --> 00:31:18.440
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

805
00:31:18.620 --> 00:31:22.500
So next, we go back to the office, and Jim and Kelly are in the kitchen.
接下来，我们回到办公室，吉姆和凯莉在厨房里。

806
00:31:22.860 --> 00:31:25.780
I love this scene so much.
我太喜欢这一幕了。

807
00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:28.960
John Krasinski, your acting in this scene is delicious.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基，你在这场戏里的表演真是太棒了。

808
00:31:29.240 --> 00:31:29.860
It's delicious.
真是太棒了。

809
00:31:30.340 --> 00:31:31.940
Mindy's acting is delicious.
敏迪的表演也太棒了。

810
00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:32.600
So good.
太好了。

811
00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:34.800
I was like, she's so funny in it.
我当时就想，她在戏里太搞笑了。

812
00:31:35.020 --> 00:31:36.180
She's full on Mindy.
她完全就是敏迪本人。

813
00:31:36.280 --> 00:31:37.100
Yeah, it's full Mindy.
没错，完全是敏迪。

814
00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:38.320
This is full Mindy.
这就是纯粹的敏迪。

815
00:31:38.460 --> 00:31:48.000
I want you to know, when I was listening to the DVD commentary, I almost, like, spit out, like, the water I was drinking because Greg and Mike both go, oh, I mean,
我想让你知道，当我听DVD评论音轨时，我差点把喝的水喷出来，因为格雷格和迈克都说，哦，我的意思是，

816
00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:49.220
Mindy just took over.
敏迪完全接管了角色。

817
00:31:49.420 --> 00:31:50.960
Like, there's no more Kelly.
就像，已经没有凯莉了。

818
00:31:51.120 --> 00:31:51.760
It's just Mindy.
只有敏迪。

819
00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:52.860
This was a whole thing.
这可是件大事。

820
00:31:53.020 --> 00:31:55.360
Yeah, what they don't know is that it happened last episode.
是啊，他们不知道的是，这事在上集就发生了。

821
00:31:55.360 --> 00:32:02.380
Okay, well, I felt very validated that we didn't even know that, like, they totally talk about it in the commentary.
好吧，我感到非常欣慰，因为我们甚至都不知道这一点，他们在评论音轨里完全谈到了它。

822
00:32:02.580 --> 00:32:03.200
That's amazing.
那太神奇了。

823
00:32:03.520 --> 00:32:08.820
Well, basically, she tells Jim that her and Ryan hooked up last night.
嗯，基本上，她告诉吉姆她和瑞安昨晚好上了。

824
00:32:08.820 --> 00:32:19.320
Yes, and Mindy says in the DVD commentary, she goes, Mike, I really feel like this scene is just like a transcription of a conversation you and I actually had about a guy.
是的，敏迪在DVD评论音轨里说，她说，迈克，我真的觉得这一幕就像是你和我实际上关于一个男人的谈话记录。

825
00:32:20.400 --> 00:32:21.640
Which cracked me up.
这让我笑喷了。

826
00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:24.900
Well, it leads to the very famous Ryan talking head.
嗯，这引出了非常著名的瑞安访谈片段。

827
00:32:25.580 --> 00:32:29.100
I hooked up with her on February 13th.
我在2月13号和她好上了。

828
00:32:29.180 --> 00:32:29.560
I know.
我知道。

829
00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:30.880
It was, like, so perfect.
这简直太完美了。

830
00:32:31.860 --> 00:32:32.540
All right.
好吧。

831
00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:37.180
So then we head back to New York City again, and now we're going to see Michael in Times Square.
然后我们再次回到纽约市，现在我们要看迈克尔在时代广场了。

832
00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:43.920
You know, a lot of people, he tells you, they get to New York and they go to really touristy places, like the Empire State Building.
你知道，很多人，他告诉你，他们到了纽约会去非常游客的地方，比如帝国大厦。

833
00:32:44.300 --> 00:32:46.680
But he likes to go to Times Square.
但他喜欢去时代广场。

834
00:32:47.280 --> 00:32:50.480
He likes to go to the most tourist spot in New York.
他喜欢去纽约最游客的地方。

835
00:32:50.480 --> 00:32:51.780
Which I love.
这一点我很喜欢。

836
00:32:51.980 --> 00:32:57.900
And then at 5 minutes, 26 seconds, Michael is giving us a tour of Rockefeller Center.
然后在5分26秒，迈克尔带我们参观洛克菲勒中心。

837
00:32:58.160 --> 00:32:58.640
Yes.
是的。

838
00:32:58.860 --> 00:33:05.520
Where he says, founded, of course, by Theodore Rockefeller, and he also says that the rangers sometimes practice there.
他说，当然是由西奥多·洛克菲勒创立的，他还说游骑兵队有时会在那里练习。

839
00:33:05.960 --> 00:33:08.180
Okay, I did a deep dive.
好吧，我深入研究了一下。

840
00:33:08.300 --> 00:33:09.720
The rangers don't practice there.
游骑兵队不在那里练习。

841
00:33:09.840 --> 00:33:14.260
The rangers don't practice there, but they do sometimes practice at this rink in Central Park.
游骑兵队不在那里练习，但他们有时确实会在中央公园的这个溜冰场练习。

842
00:33:14.440 --> 00:33:16.360
Like, once a year, there's a rink there.
就像，一年一次，那里有个溜冰场。

843
00:33:16.360 --> 00:33:22.000
I know this because I have a huge hockey, yeah, I'm a hockey mom.
我知道这一点是因为我非常喜欢冰球，是的，我是个冰球妈妈。

844
00:33:22.300 --> 00:33:23.420
Your husband plays hockey.
你丈夫打冰球。

845
00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:24.280
Your son plays hockey.
你儿子打冰球。

846
00:33:24.380 --> 00:33:25.080
You're a hockey mom.
你是个冰球妈妈。

847
00:33:25.220 --> 00:33:25.480
Yes.
是的。

848
00:33:25.640 --> 00:33:30.020
We've been in New York when the rangers have practiced on this rink in Central Park, and it's super cool.
我们曾在游骑兵队在中央公园这个溜冰场练习时去过纽约，这太酷了。

849
00:33:30.180 --> 00:33:31.480
It's a thing they do for the fans.
这是他们为粉丝做的一件事。

850
00:33:32.120 --> 00:33:33.940
But never at Rockefeller Center.
但从不在洛克菲勒中心。

851
00:33:34.160 --> 00:33:37.400
Also, there is no one named Theodore Rockefeller.
另外，根本没有叫西奥多·洛克菲勒的人。

852
00:33:38.100 --> 00:33:43.260
I did a deep dive on the Rockefeller family, and I could not find anyone named Theodore.
我深入研究了洛克菲勒家族，但我找不到任何叫西奥多的人。

853
00:33:43.660 --> 00:33:47.080
Okay, I know 30 Rock really well because I worked there.
好吧，我对《我为喜剧狂》非常了解，因为我曾在那里工作过。

854
00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:48.740
Oh, that's right.
哦，没错。

855
00:33:48.760 --> 00:33:50.880
I was an intern on the Conan O'Brien show.
我曾是柯南·奥布莱恩节目的实习生。

856
00:33:51.200 --> 00:33:53.220
And so were like a bunch of office people.
还有很多办公室的人也是。

857
00:33:53.400 --> 00:33:55.080
Mindy, Ellie, John.
敏迪、艾莉、约翰。

858
00:33:55.360 --> 00:33:56.180
But not at the same time.
但不是同一时间。

859
00:33:56.200 --> 00:33:56.900
Not at the same time.
不是同一时间。

860
00:33:56.900 --> 00:33:58.660
I'm much older than those guys.
我比他们大得多。

861
00:33:58.860 --> 00:34:03.380
I was there the very first year of Conan when they thought they were going to get canceled week to week.
我在柯南节目开播的第一年就在那里了，当时他们以为随时会被砍掉。

862
00:34:03.600 --> 00:34:04.580
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

863
00:34:05.420 --> 00:34:08.340
What do you do when you're an intern on that?
当那里的实习生是做什么的？

864
00:34:08.560 --> 00:34:09.380
Like, what is that?
那是什么样的工作？

865
00:34:09.540 --> 00:34:10.500
Well, there was –
嗯，有——

866
00:34:10.500 --> 00:34:11.180
What does that mean?
那是什么意思？

867
00:34:11.360 --> 00:34:12.700
Well, there was different types of internships.
嗯，实习生有不同类型。

868
00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:14.060
Like, there was a writer's intern.
比如，有编剧实习生。

869
00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:16.800
So when I got the internship, they already had the writer's intern.
所以我拿到实习机会时，他们已经有编剧实习生了。

870
00:34:17.160 --> 00:34:18.880
So I became a general intern.
所以我成了普通实习生。

871
00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:21.160
So I just basically got everyone their coffee.
基本上就是帮大家买咖啡。

872
00:34:21.880 --> 00:34:24.860
And I didn't know New York City, so I kept getting loSt.
而且我不熟悉纽约市，所以总是迷路。

873
00:34:24.860 --> 00:34:28.020
I was probably the worst coffee-run person ever.
我大概是有史以来最差劲的跑腿买咖啡的人了。

874
00:34:28.260 --> 00:34:31.360
Did you get to meet Conan or interact with him as an intern?
你作为实习生有机会见到柯南或与他互动吗？

875
00:34:31.440 --> 00:34:33.380
I didn't – I mean, he would walk paSt.
我没有——我是说，他会走过去。

876
00:34:33.520 --> 00:34:34.380
And he was always nice.
他总是很友善。

877
00:34:34.400 --> 00:34:35.980
He would kind of give a nod or a wave.
他会点头或挥手示意。

878
00:34:36.020 --> 00:34:37.300
But he was busy, you know?
但他很忙，你知道吧？

879
00:34:37.340 --> 00:34:37.480
Yeah.
是的。

880
00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:38.780
And I knew not to bug him.
而且我知道不要去打扰他。

881
00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:42.180
Like, I had enough, like, awareness that I wasn't going to be like,
我有足够的自觉，不会像那样去说，

882
00:34:42.220 --> 00:34:43.480
Hey, Conan, I'm the new intern.
嘿，柯南，我是新来的实习生。

883
00:34:43.480 --> 00:34:43.980
What you doing?
你在忙什么？

884
00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:50.280
The really cool thing about Conan Studio is it was one floor away from where they did Saturday Night Live.
柯南演播室最酷的地方在于，它离《周六夜现场》的录制地只有一层之隔。

885
00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:51.520
So could you –
所以你能——

886
00:34:51.520 --> 00:34:52.540
You could do a backdoor –
你可以走后门——

887
00:34:52.540 --> 00:34:54.100
Like, watch SNL ever?
比如，看过《周六夜现场》吗？

888
00:34:54.100 --> 00:35:00.360
I actually – one of the people that worked on Conan knew that I was pretty strapped for cash.
其实——柯南节目组的一个人知道我当时手头很紧。

889
00:35:00.480 --> 00:35:03.820
And she got me a weekend job on Saturday Night Live as an extra.
她帮我在《周六夜现场》找了一份周末临时演员的工作。

890
00:35:04.040 --> 00:35:09.180
So there's a whole season of SNL that I'm an extra, and I'm in a bunch of skits.
所以有一整季的《周六夜现场》我都在当临时演员，还参与了好几个小品。

891
00:35:09.340 --> 00:35:09.660
What?
什么？

892
00:35:09.920 --> 00:35:10.340
Yes.
是的。

893
00:35:10.420 --> 00:35:14.560
There's a great scene with Chris Farley, and I'm, like, sitting in front of him.
有一个很棒的场景是和克里斯·法利一起拍的，我就坐在他前面。

894
00:35:14.620 --> 00:35:16.440
And everyone was so nice.
每个人都特别好。

895
00:35:16.700 --> 00:35:19.400
Yeah, because all that stuff is happening in that same building.
是啊，因为所有那些节目都在同一栋楼里制作。

896
00:35:19.620 --> 00:35:21.760
That's what's so crazy about that area.
那片区域最疯狂的地方就在于此。

897
00:35:21.760 --> 00:35:24.860
And, like, NBC News is happening, and the Today Show.
NBC新闻和《今日秀》也都在那里。

898
00:35:24.860 --> 00:35:26.180
It's all right there.
全都在那儿。

899
00:35:26.400 --> 00:35:28.180
Can I tell you one of the coolest moments?
我能告诉你一个最酷的时刻吗？

900
00:35:28.460 --> 00:35:28.620
What?
什么？

901
00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:33.320
Is right outside the stage doors where we recorded, I'm standing in this hallway alone.
就在我们录制节目的演播室门外，我独自站在走廊里。

902
00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:35.200
There's no one in the hallway.
走廊里一个人都没有。

903
00:35:35.400 --> 00:35:38.920
The elevator doors open, and Robert Redford walked out.
电梯门开了，罗伯特·雷德福走了出来。

904
00:35:39.640 --> 00:35:40.200
Wow.
哇。

905
00:35:40.600 --> 00:35:44.800
And he was with, like, an NBC, you know, someone in a suit, and they were walking down the hall.
他当时和NBC的一个人在一起，你知道的，就是那种穿西装的人，他们正沿着走廊走。

906
00:35:45.100 --> 00:35:47.940
And they just walked past me, and I was just like, bleh.
他们就这么从我身边走过，我当时整个人都呆住了。

907
00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:51.660
Just watched Robert Redford walk right by.
就这么看着罗伯特·雷德福从我身边走过。

908
00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:52.360
Wow.
哇。

909
00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:55.380
I'm just, like, a young kid from middle of nowhere, Texas.
我当时只是个来自德克萨斯州偏远地区的毛头小子。

910
00:35:55.620 --> 00:35:58.160
It was just, like, a really cool, surreal moment.
那真是一个非常酷、非常超现实的时刻。

911
00:35:58.220 --> 00:36:00.360
And there were many of those in my time there.
我在那儿的时候，经历过很多这样的时刻。

912
00:36:00.620 --> 00:36:01.800
That is pretty awesome.
那真是太棒了。

913
00:36:02.370 --> 00:36:06.920
So, we got a lot of fan questions about this Tina Fey, Conan O'Brien business.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于蒂娜·菲和柯南·奥布莱恩这件事的提问。

914
00:36:07.260 --> 00:36:07.400
Yeah.
没错。

915
00:36:07.520 --> 00:36:09.440
The first one is from Sarah Marshall, 44.
第一个问题来自44岁的莎拉·马歇尔。

916
00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:14.060
Did production hire the woman to play the fake Tina Fey, or was she just a random person?
制作组是专门雇人来演假蒂娜·菲的，还是随便找的路人？

917
00:36:14.340 --> 00:36:14.800
No.
不是。

918
00:36:14.940 --> 00:36:15.780
We hired her.
是我们雇的她。

919
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:18.180
She is an actress named Miriam Tolan.
她是一位名叫米里亚姆·托兰的演员。

920
00:36:18.440 --> 00:36:23.900
She's been in a ton of stuff, including, ironically, an episode of 30 Rock.
她演过很多作品，讽刺的是，其中就包括一集《我为喜剧狂》。

921
00:36:24.340 --> 00:36:26.140
Season 2, episode 14.
第二季第14集。

922
00:36:26.140 --> 00:36:29.680
She has a really funny scene with Jason Sotakis, around 12 minutes.
她在第12分钟左右和杰森·苏戴奇斯有一场非常有趣的戏。

923
00:36:30.020 --> 00:36:33.420
She plays a woman at a check-in counter at an airline.
她饰演航空公司值机柜台的一名女子。

924
00:36:33.780 --> 00:36:34.780
It's very funny.
非常搞笑。

925
00:36:35.180 --> 00:36:36.720
I went back and watched the whole episode.
我回去把整集都看了一遍。

926
00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:37.140
Oh, I want to see it.
哦，我也想看看。

927
00:36:37.140 --> 00:36:37.820
It's really good.
真的很好看。

928
00:36:37.820 --> 00:36:38.060
I want to see it.
我也想看。

929
00:36:38.280 --> 00:36:40.800
And then we had another fan question from Livvy Fitzgerald.
然后我们还有另一个来自利维·菲茨杰拉德的粉丝提问。

930
00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:43.900
Please explain the Conan cameo.
请解释一下柯南的客串。

931
00:36:44.460 --> 00:36:46.980
Well, you know, Greg and Conan were very good friends.
嗯，你知道，格雷格和柯南是非常好的朋友。

932
00:36:47.140 --> 00:36:48.180
They went to college together.
他们大学时就在一起。

933
00:36:48.340 --> 00:36:49.120
They were roommates.
他们是室友。

934
00:36:49.500 --> 00:36:54.640
I think some of their very early writing jobs on SNL and Simpsons, they were, like, they lived together.
我想他们早期在《周六夜现场》和《辛普森一家》做编剧时，他们就住在一起。

935
00:36:54.780 --> 00:36:55.160
They're friends.
他们是朋友。

936
00:36:55.160 --> 00:36:56.280
They're really good friends.
他们是非常好的朋友。

937
00:36:56.480 --> 00:37:01.800
And so it definitely makes sense that Greg, you know, would want to reach out to Conan if he was right there.
所以格雷格如果就在附近，想要联系柯南绝对合情合理。

938
00:37:02.100 --> 00:37:04.500
There is quite a bit about it in the DVD commentary.
DVD评论音轨里对此有不少介绍。

939
00:37:04.820 --> 00:37:12.780
But one of the things that really stuck with me that I loved is that Greg said it took Conan 15 takes to time that out.
但有一件事让我印象深刻，我也很喜欢，那就是格雷格说柯南拍了15条才把时间卡准。

940
00:37:13.060 --> 00:37:15.220
Like, he said literally it took about 15 tries.
他说真的拍了大约15次。

941
00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:17.760
And he said, you think Steve gets a big crowd?
他还说，你以为史蒂夫那边人很多吗？

942
00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:21.380
Imagine Conan standing in front of the building where they taped Conan.
想象一下柯南站在录制《柯南秀》的大楼前。

943
00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:21.820
Yeah.
没错。

944
00:37:22.060 --> 00:37:25.020
He said the crowds were crazy, so they were trying to get that.
他说当时人群太疯狂了，所以他们一直在努力捕捉那个镜头。

945
00:37:25.160 --> 00:37:26.240
And he's really tall.
而且他真的很高。

