1106
00:43:35.130 --> 00:43:36.530
And he was a friend of Mike's.
而且他是迈克的挚友。

1107
00:43:36.610 --> 00:43:38.950
And Mindy sort of chimed in that Mike loved to do that.
明迪也附和说迈克很喜欢那样做。

1108
00:43:39.050 --> 00:43:41.310
He loved to put his friends' names in things.
他喜欢把朋友的名字写进作品里。

1109
00:43:41.810 --> 00:43:42.970
He was a Conan writer.
他曾是《柯南秀》的编剧。

1110
00:43:42.990 --> 00:43:44.210
He wrote on Parks and Rec.
他曾为《公园与游憩》写过剧本。

1111
00:43:44.210 --> 00:43:47.150
And now, of course, he's the showrunner of Brooklyn Nine-Nine.
当然，现在他是《神烦警探》的剧集运作人。

1112
00:43:47.350 --> 00:43:50.270
So Dan Gore got a nice little shout out in this episode.
所以丹·戈尔在这一集中得到了一个小小的致敬。

1113
00:43:50.470 --> 00:43:50.790
Yes.
是的。

1114
00:43:50.990 --> 00:43:52.890
So we are meeting all the Branch Heads.
我们正在见所有的分部主管。

1115
00:43:53.350 --> 00:43:54.790
And Craigers is an idiot.
而克雷格是个白痴。

1116
00:43:55.010 --> 00:43:55.710
He's, right?
他是，对吧？

1117
00:43:55.870 --> 00:43:58.470
He's gotten kicked out of all the strip clubs in Albany.
他被奥尔巴尼所有的脱衣舞俱乐部赶了出来。

1118
00:43:58.630 --> 00:43:59.490
Very proud of that.
对此他引以为傲。

1119
00:43:59.630 --> 00:43:59.870
We find out.
我们发现了这一点。

1120
00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:01.890
And then he starts insulting Jan.
然后他开始侮辱简。

1121
00:44:02.110 --> 00:44:02.450
Yeah.
没错。

1122
00:44:02.830 --> 00:44:03.070
Yeah.
没错。

1123
00:44:03.210 --> 00:44:03.990
He says.
他说。

1124
00:44:04.230 --> 00:44:05.790
He calls her the B word.
他骂她是那个B开头的词。

1125
00:44:05.790 --> 00:44:06.410
He does.
他确实说了。

1126
00:44:06.410 --> 00:44:08.230
And Michael comes to her defense.
迈克尔站出来维护她。

1127
00:44:08.230 --> 00:44:09.410
He says, oh, come on now.
他说，噢，得了吧。

1128
00:44:09.510 --> 00:44:09.930
Come on now.
得了吧。

1129
00:44:09.930 --> 00:44:13.610
And he stands up for her first by saying, that's my girlfriend.
他先是说“那是我女朋友”来维护她。

1130
00:44:14.350 --> 00:44:14.790
Boy.
天哪。

1131
00:44:15.030 --> 00:44:17.430
And then he backpedals and says, I mean, we hooked up.
然后他又改口说，我是说，我们有过一腿。

1132
00:44:17.650 --> 00:44:20.270
And then Josh Porter's like, you hooked up with Jan?
接着乔什·波特就问，你和简有过一腿？

1133
00:44:21.010 --> 00:44:22.550
And now he's in it.
现在他陷入麻烦了。

1134
00:44:22.690 --> 00:44:23.770
He spilled the beans.
他把秘密泄露了。

1135
00:44:23.910 --> 00:44:24.770
Dang it, Michael.
该死，迈克尔。

1136
00:44:24.970 --> 00:44:25.410
Michael.
迈克尔啊。

1137
00:44:25.670 --> 00:44:27.670
He's only been there like five minutes.
他才在那儿待了五分钟左右。

1138
00:44:27.930 --> 00:44:28.110
Yeah.
没错。

1139
00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:30.390
He's been in a room with these people for five minutes.
他和这些人待在一个房间里才五分钟。

1140
00:44:30.390 --> 00:44:33.530
And he's already told everyone that he's hooked up with Jan.
就已经告诉所有人他和简有过一腿了。

1141
00:44:33.730 --> 00:44:34.490
With their boss.
和他们的老板。

1142
00:44:34.710 --> 00:44:34.970
Yeah.
没错。

1143
00:44:35.110 --> 00:44:35.730
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1144
00:44:35.990 --> 00:44:37.730
And then it's like crickets in the room.
然后房间里一片死寂。

1145
00:44:38.110 --> 00:44:38.450
All right.
好吧。

1146
00:44:38.450 --> 00:44:40.050
Well, maybe we should take a break.
也许我们该休息一下了。

1147
00:44:40.210 --> 00:44:40.570
Yeah.
没错。

1148
00:44:40.670 --> 00:44:41.930
With that news.
带着这个消息。

1149
00:44:42.050 --> 00:44:44.630
On that news, Michael has just spilled the beans.
在这个消息之后，迈克尔刚刚把秘密泄露了。

1150
00:44:44.810 --> 00:44:45.930
And we'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1151
00:44:45.930 --> 00:44:50.550
Well, because one of my favorite scenes is happening back at the office.
因为我最喜欢的场景之一正在办公室里上演。

1152
00:44:50.750 --> 00:44:50.910
Yeah.
没错。

1153
00:44:51.070 --> 00:44:52.030
We need to talk about it.
我们需要谈谈这件事。

1154
00:44:52.050 --> 00:44:52.430
It's good stuff.
这很有意思。

1155
00:44:52.590 --> 00:44:52.930
It's good.
挺好的。

1156
00:44:57.760 --> 00:44:58.160
Okay.
好的。

1157
00:44:58.160 --> 00:44:58.880
So we're back.
我们回来了。

1158
00:44:59.020 --> 00:45:04.260
You guys, I have to talk about this scene between Dwight and Pam in the break room.
伙计们，我得聊聊休息室里德怀特和帕姆的那场戏。

1159
00:45:04.420 --> 00:45:04.560
Yeah.
没错。

1160
00:45:04.640 --> 00:45:06.940
I loved it so much, Jenna.
我太喜欢那场戏了，珍娜。

1161
00:45:07.180 --> 00:45:09.100
I rewound and watched it a few times.
我倒回去看了好几遍。

1162
00:45:10.400 --> 00:45:11.200
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1163
00:45:11.200 --> 00:45:12.960
How did you get through it without laughing?
你是怎么忍住没笑场的？

1164
00:45:13.220 --> 00:45:13.400
How?
怎么做到的？

1165
00:45:13.660 --> 00:45:17.340
Your reaction when he says, like a ham?
当他说“像火腿一样”时，你的反应。

1166
00:45:17.520 --> 00:45:17.780
Yeah.
没错。

1167
00:45:17.940 --> 00:45:20.300
And you're like, no, not exactly like a ham.
你说“不，不完全像火腿”。

1168
00:45:20.720 --> 00:45:21.720
Jenna, it's so funny.
珍娜，那太搞笑了。

1169
00:45:21.840 --> 00:45:23.400
I don't even know how you kept a straight face, though.
我真不知道你是怎么忍住不笑的。

1170
00:45:23.860 --> 00:45:28.860
My intention in that was like I was talking to like a five or a six-year-old.
我当时的想法是，我就像在跟一个五六岁的孩子说话。

1171
00:45:28.860 --> 00:45:36.040
And I couldn't let them see my real feelings about the things they were saying.
我不能让他们看出我对他们所说的话的真实感受。

1172
00:45:36.280 --> 00:45:36.760
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1173
00:45:37.180 --> 00:45:39.660
We had a fan question from Susie Young, 22.
我们收到了来自22岁的苏西·杨的粉丝提问。

1174
00:45:39.980 --> 00:45:43.240
She wanted to know if like a ham was scripted or improvised.
她想知道“像火腿一样”这句台词是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

1175
00:45:43.260 --> 00:45:44.440
It was improvised.
是即兴发挥的。

1176
00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:45.780
Did he improvise a bunch?
他即兴发挥了很多吗？

1177
00:45:46.020 --> 00:45:46.240
Yeah.
是的。

1178
00:45:46.480 --> 00:45:50.760
So on the day, we didn't really have an ending to this scene.
拍摄当天，我们其实并没有给这场戏设计结尾。

1179
00:45:50.940 --> 00:45:51.260
Okay.
好的。

1180
00:45:51.260 --> 00:45:56.020
We had him coming in and asking for advice, and they wanted a button.
剧本里是他进来寻求建议，他们想要一个收尾。

1181
00:45:56.220 --> 00:45:57.700
And this would often happen in scenes.
这种情况在拍摄中经常发生。

1182
00:45:57.900 --> 00:46:02.300
And the writers would then come over and give us a list of options.
编剧们会走过来给我们提供一堆选项。

1183
00:46:02.300 --> 00:46:03.040
Like suggestions.
就像建议一样。

1184
00:46:03.460 --> 00:46:03.660
Yeah.
没错。

1185
00:46:04.280 --> 00:46:06.340
So like a ham was improvised.
所以“像火腿一样”是即兴的。

1186
00:46:06.520 --> 00:46:10.120
But then there were all these other options that were written on a piece of paper.
但纸上还写着其他所有的选项。

1187
00:46:10.320 --> 00:46:14.760
And so we shot all of these things that he said.
所以我们把他说过的那些话都拍了一遍。

1188
00:46:14.960 --> 00:46:17.520
Like a this, like a that, like this, like that.
像这个，像那个，像这样，像那样。

1189
00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:20.340
It was so hard not to laugh.
忍住不笑真的太难了。

1190
00:46:20.780 --> 00:46:24.220
I did laugh at like a ham because it wasn't on the piece of paper.
我确实在“像火腿一样”那句笑场了，因为它不在纸上。

1191
00:46:24.300 --> 00:46:25.700
So I was not expecting it.
所以我完全没预料到。

1192
00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:25.960
You didn't see it coming.
你没料到他会这么说。

1193
00:46:26.060 --> 00:46:26.280
No.
没有。

1194
00:46:26.480 --> 00:46:26.860
No.
没有。

1195
00:46:26.980 --> 00:46:30.720
So that my response is definitely like take four or five.
所以我的反应肯定是第四或第五条拍摄时的版本。

1196
00:46:30.960 --> 00:46:34.100
Because I remember everyone just lost it when he said it.
因为我记得他一说出口，大家就都笑喷了。

1197
00:46:34.300 --> 00:46:36.460
And then they were like, okay, wait, that's good.
然后他们说，好吧，等等，这个好。

1198
00:46:36.520 --> 00:46:36.880
That's good.
这个好。

1199
00:46:36.940 --> 00:46:37.680
That's the one we want.
我们要的就是这个。

1200
00:46:37.820 --> 00:46:40.320
And so then they were like, pull it together.
于是他们说，收敛一下。

1201
00:46:40.700 --> 00:46:41.620
And do it again.
再来一遍。

1202
00:46:41.820 --> 00:46:42.320
Do it again.
再来一次。

1203
00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:42.700
Okay.
好的。

1204
00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:43.760
I have a question for you.
我有个问题要问你。

1205
00:46:43.860 --> 00:46:46.160
When he says, shut up, I know exactly what to do.
当他说闭嘴时，我完全知道该怎么做。

1206
00:46:46.240 --> 00:46:47.220
Was that improvised?
那是即兴发挥的吗？

1207
00:46:47.220 --> 00:46:48.440
That I don't remember.
那我不记得了。

1208
00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:54.580
I don't remember because I do think that that final look to camera was, that was some direction I was given.
我不记得了，因为我觉得最后看向镜头的那个眼神，那是导演给我的指示。

1209
00:46:54.960 --> 00:46:57.840
Which is like, I know the camera's out there.
就像是，我知道摄像机在那儿。

1210
00:46:57.960 --> 00:46:58.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1211
00:46:58.300 --> 00:47:00.800
And your look to camera's like, can this day get any worse?
而你看向镜头的眼神就像在说，今天还能再糟糕点吗？

1212
00:47:00.980 --> 00:47:01.640
It's so weird.
太奇怪了。

1213
00:47:01.700 --> 00:47:02.900
I'm not getting any gifts.
我什么礼物都没收到。

1214
00:47:03.140 --> 00:47:03.280
No.
没有。

1215
00:47:03.600 --> 00:47:05.160
Jim has barely acknowledged me.
吉姆几乎没理过我。

1216
00:47:05.300 --> 00:47:07.540
And Dwight just asked for my help and then told me to shut up.
德怀特刚找我帮忙，然后又叫我闭嘴。

1217
00:47:07.540 --> 00:47:15.160
I also love when Rain, how Rain responds to me saying, like, she's a little, like, tightly wound.
我也很喜欢雷恩，喜欢雷恩对我说她有点神经紧绷时的反应。

1218
00:47:15.200 --> 00:47:15.520
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1219
00:47:15.520 --> 00:47:16.780
And he's like, yeah.
然后他说，是啊。

1220
00:47:17.080 --> 00:47:19.200
He, like, chose to be, like, turned on by it.
他好像选择被这种状态吸引了。

1221
00:47:19.280 --> 00:47:20.000
It's so gross.
太恶心了。

1222
00:47:20.160 --> 00:47:20.740
Kind of creepy.
有点变态。

1223
00:47:20.740 --> 00:47:25.660
Did you notice how many times we were in scenes in the break room in the kitchen?
你注意到我们在休息室和厨房的场景有多少次了吗？

1224
00:47:26.220 --> 00:47:28.500
Like, in this episode, we're in quite a few.
在这集里，我们有好几场戏都在那儿。

1225
00:47:28.540 --> 00:47:31.360
I think we have, like, three break room scenes, two kitchen scenes.
我想我们大概有三场休息室的戏，两场厨房的戏。

1226
00:47:31.420 --> 00:47:31.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1227
00:47:31.720 --> 00:47:37.460
So, it's interesting, and I don't know if that's because they were constantly trying to keep Jim and Pam apart.
所以这很有趣，我不知道是不是因为他们一直试图让吉姆和帕姆分开。

1228
00:47:37.620 --> 00:47:37.740
Maybe so.
也许吧。

1229
00:47:37.740 --> 00:47:40.800
Or there were these secret conversations about relationships.
或者是因为有关于感情的秘密谈话。

1230
00:47:41.340 --> 00:47:48.740
But I feel like this was a very interesting episode for that reason, because a lot of the scenes don't actually happen in the bullpen.
但我感觉这一集因为这个原因非常有趣，因为很多场景实际上并没有发生在办公区。

1231
00:47:48.980 --> 00:47:50.900
Yeah, they're not at our desks this time.
没错，这次他们不在我们的办公桌前。

1232
00:47:50.980 --> 00:47:51.200
Mm-mm.
嗯。

1233
00:47:51.480 --> 00:47:51.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1234
00:47:52.040 --> 00:47:56.920
So, Jim is in the break room with Kelly, and he's kind of trying to give her advice.
所以，吉姆和凯莉在休息室里，他正试图给她一些建议。

1235
00:47:56.920 --> 00:47:58.980
He's really just trying to eat his bag of chips.
他其实只是想吃他的薯片。

1236
00:47:59.240 --> 00:47:59.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1237
00:47:59.500 --> 00:48:03.460
So, he tells her to take it slow, and then Ryan walks in.
所以，他告诉她慢慢来，然后瑞安走了进来。

1238
00:48:03.680 --> 00:48:10.140
And she asks him out in front of Jim, and John's, the way John played this moment, like, he's like, not in front of me.
她当着吉姆的面约他，而约翰，约翰处理这一刻的方式，就像是说，别当着我的面啊。

1239
00:48:10.500 --> 00:48:12.220
He's like, oh, no, not while I'm here.
他就像在说，噢不，别在我面前这样。

1240
00:48:12.760 --> 00:48:13.720
No, I'm here, please.
不，我就在这儿，求你了。

1241
00:48:14.020 --> 00:48:15.600
Oh, so good.
噢，太棒了。

1242
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:17.400
But Ryan shoots her down.
但瑞安拒绝了她。

1243
00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:18.980
He says, I can't.
他说，我不行。

1244
00:48:19.040 --> 00:48:20.180
I have plans with friends.
我和朋友有约了。

1245
00:48:20.780 --> 00:48:21.500
I can't.
我不能去。

1246
00:48:21.580 --> 00:48:22.380
Oh, it's so cringy.
噢，太尴尬了。

1247
00:48:22.560 --> 00:48:23.320
And she's like, oh, yeah, yeah.
然后她说，噢，好的，好的。

1248
00:48:23.320 --> 00:48:23.660
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1249
00:48:23.840 --> 00:48:24.760
Yeah, no, it's not a problem.
没事，没问题。

1250
00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:25.380
Not a problem.
没问题。

1251
00:48:25.780 --> 00:48:26.060
Ugh.
呃。

1252
00:48:26.700 --> 00:48:28.360
And Jim is just sitting there.
而吉姆就坐在那儿。

1253
00:48:28.480 --> 00:48:29.240
Just sitting there.
就坐在那儿。

1254
00:48:29.500 --> 00:48:30.080
Out of here.
走人了。

1255
00:48:31.040 --> 00:48:35.100
Back in the bullpen, more gifts for Phyllis, and Meredith is drinking heavily.
回到办公区，菲利斯收到了更多礼物，而梅雷迪思喝得烂醉。

1256
00:48:35.400 --> 00:48:36.180
She's had it.
她受够了。

1257
00:48:36.380 --> 00:48:36.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1258
00:48:36.480 --> 00:48:38.600
She's full on mixing up a cocktail.
她正在大张旗鼓地调鸡尾酒呢。

1259
00:48:38.760 --> 00:48:39.380
She sure is.
确实是。

1260
00:48:39.500 --> 00:48:40.060
And that Super Gulp.
还有那个超大杯。

1261
00:48:40.280 --> 00:48:48.700
I have been to family reunions where I have one or two aunts that walk around with a giant 7-Eleven Super Gulp, and I'm always like, what's in there?
我参加过家庭聚会，总有一两个阿姨手里拿着个巨大的7-Eleven超大杯，我总是想，那里面装的是什么？

1262
00:48:49.280 --> 00:48:53.440
Why are you nursing on that 7-Eleven Super Gulp all day?
你为什么整天抱着那个7-Eleven超大杯喝个不停？

1263
00:48:53.640 --> 00:48:56.000
Well, I used to do an opposite thing in college.
嗯，我上大学时正好相反。

1264
00:48:56.220 --> 00:49:01.260
So I was not a big drinker, but I wanted to go to the parties and not be judged.
我不太爱喝酒，但我又想去参加派对，不想被人评头论足。

1265
00:49:01.260 --> 00:49:03.940
So you'd bring a Super Gulp full of, like, soda?
所以你就带个装满汽水的超大杯去？

1266
00:49:04.160 --> 00:49:06.920
I would bring a red Solo Cup full.
我会带个装满饮料的红色塑料杯。

1267
00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:09.080
Your own Solo Cup to the party?
你自己带塑料杯去派对？

1268
00:49:09.080 --> 00:49:10.420
Your own red Solo Cup.
你自己带的红色塑料杯。

1269
00:49:10.600 --> 00:49:14.120
And then I would put something non-alcoholic in it.
然后我会在里面装上非酒精饮料。

1270
00:49:14.180 --> 00:49:15.220
And you'd be like, I'm good.
然后你就会装作，我挺好的。

1271
00:49:15.220 --> 00:49:15.660
I've got my drink.
